- Amount of time spent reading books per day: More time spent reading likely correlates positively with reading academic books most of the time.  
- Reason for reading books: If the reason is "Academic Purpose," more likely to read academic books most of the time; other reasons (Entertainment, Informative, Vocabulary) less likely.  
- How to manage books for reading: Methods like "Buy," "Used-all," or "Borrow" might indicate more serious reading habits; "E-books" or "Others" less indicative.  
