- Number of printed books read last two years: Similarly, higher number suggests more reading activity.  
- Favorite books for leisure time: If favorite leisure books are "Non-Fiction" or "Biography," may indicate academic interest; "Fiction," "Politics," or "Others" less so.  
- What is the change felt after reading books: "Increase Academic Performance" or "Increase Problem Solving Skill" indicates academic reading; "Feel Relax" or "Increase Creative Thinking" less so.  
- Who influenced you to read books: "Teachers" or "Self-Decision" may indicate academic motivation; "Friends" or "Parents" less so.  
